7,"Lyndon B. Johnson also took over after a sudden death, but the transition happened in front of cameras."],[5.65,"After Kennedy was assassinated in Dallas in 1963, Johnson took the oath aboard Air Force One."],[11.79,"Jacqueline Kennedy stood beside him, with Kennedy's casket elsewhere on the plane."],[16.27,"Johnson used his congressional experience to help secure the Civil Rights Act and Voting Rights Act, and he won the 1964 election."],[24.1,"His escalation of the Vietnam War helped tear apart his presidency."],[27.86,"In 1968, he announced he wouldn't seek another term."],[31.53,"Richard Nixon had spent eight years as Eisenhower's vice president, then lost the 1960 election to Kennedy."],[37.69,"Two years later, he lost the California governor's race as well."],[40.97,"His career seemed to be running backward."],[43.15,"Then he won the presidency in 1968."],[46.44,"Eight years as vice president, eight years out of office, then the top job."],[50.44,"Watergate eventually destroyed that comeback."],[53.15,"In 1974, Nixon became the first U.S. president to resign."],[57.83,"Which brings us to Gerald Ford."],[60.06,"Nixon's original vice president, Spiro Agnew, had already resigned."],[64.12,"Nixon nominated Ford to replace him, and Congress confirmed him."],[67.92,"Eight months later, Nixon resigned too."],[70.38,"Ford became president without winning an election for either national office."],[74.57,"A month afterward, he pardoned Nixon, igniting another political firestorm."],[78.87,"He tried to move the country past Watergate, but the pardon followed him into his losing campaign against Jimmy Carter."],[85.09,"George H.W. Bush took a more familiar route."],[88.5,"After eight years as Ronald Reagan's vice president, he won the 1988 election."],[93.3,"He was the first sitting vice president to win since Van Buren, a gap of 152 years."],[99.24,"Bush led the coalition that drove Iraqi forces out of Kuwait."],[102.9,"At home, he agreed to a budget deal that raised taxes after campaigning against new ones."],[107.76,"His foreign-policy success didn't secure another term."],[111.27,"Bill Clinton defeated him in 1992."]],"words":[["lyndon",0,0.07],["b",0,0.38],["johnson",0,0.53],["also",0,0.98],["took",0,1.44],["over",0,1.67],["after",0,1.97],["a",0,2.28],["sudden",0,2.31],["death",0,2.67],["but",0,3.08],["the",0,3.25],["transition",0,3.32],["happened",0,3.91],["in",0,4.28],["front",0,4.38],["of",0,4.55],["cameras",0,4.62],["after",1,5.65],["kennedy",1,5.99],["was",1,6.34],["assassinated",1,6.5],["in",1,7.16],["dallas",1,7.28],["in",1,7.71],["1963",1,7.78],["johnson",1,9.02],["took",1,9.49],["the",1,9.69],["oath",1,9.86],["aboard",1,10.01],["air",1,10.35],["force",1,10.53],["one",1,10.85],["jacqueline",2,11.79],["kennedy",2,12.33],["stood",2,12.72],["beside",2,12.98],["him",2,13.39],["with",2,13.63],["kennedy's",2,13.77],["casket",2,14.2],["elsewhere",2,14.69],["on",2,15.03],["the",2,15.12],["plane",2,15.19],["johnson",3,16.27],["used",3,16.73],["his",3,16.92],["congressional",3,17.08],["experience",3,17.6],["to",3,18.1],["help",3,18.2],["secure",3,18.38],["the",3,18.85],["civil",3,18.96],["rights",3,19.27],["act",3,19.56],["and",3,19.8],["voting",3,19.93],["rights",3,20.2],["act",3,20.46],["and",3,21.38],["he",3,21.61],["won",3,21.79],["the",3,22.15],["1964",3,22.21],["election",3,23.22],["his",4,24.1],["escalation",4,24.26],["of",4,24.89],["the",4,24.96],["vietnam",4,25.03],["war",4,25.55],["helped",4,25.82],["tear",4,26.08],["apart",4,26.35],["his",4,26.67],["presidency",4,26.86],["in",5,27.86],["1968",5,27.98],["he",5,29.11],["announced",5,29.29],["he",5,29.71],["wouldn't",5,29.81],["seek",5,30.16],["another",5,30.55],["term",5,30.86],["richard",6,31.53],["nixon",6,31.83],["had",6,32.19],["spent",6,32.35],["eight",6,32.74],["years",6,32.94],["as",6,33.34],["eisenhower's",6,33.46],["vice",6,34.0],["president",6,34.24],["then",6,34.93],["lost",6,35.03],["the",6,35.42],["1960",6,35.5],["election",6,36.23],["to",6,36.69],["kenne